# Dynamic Configuration System

Pocketknife uses a three-tier configuration system for runtime flexibility:

| Layer | Service | Purpose | Use When |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Config** | `configService` | Simple key-value settings | Timeouts, limits, API URLs, defaults |
| **Rules** | `ruleEngineService` | Conditional business logic | Scoring, filtering, validation, notifications |
| **Flags** | `featureFlagService` | Feature toggles & rollouts | A/B tests, gradual rollouts, kill switches |

## 🚫 NEVER Hardcode These Values

| Type | Example | Correct Approach |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Timeouts | `timeout: 5000` | `configService.get('api.timeoutMs', 5000)` |
| Limits | `take: 100` | `configService.get('jobs.saved.maxResults', 100)` |
| AI Tokens | `maxTokens: 1500` | `configService.get('shopping.ai.maxTokens', 1500)` |
| Thresholds | `if (score > 80)` | Use Rule Engine for conditional logic |
| Feature toggles | `if (isNewFeature)` | `featureFlagService.isEnabled('new_feature')` |
| **Company Lists** | `const companies = [...]` | Store in `ExternalCompany` DB table |
| **External Data** | `const sites = [...]` | Store in database, use discovery |

> **Note**: For external entity data (companies, scrapers, products), see the **data-driven-architecture.mdc** rule for database patterns.

