## 1. ConfigService (Simple Values)

### Usage

```typescript
import { configService } from '../services/core/configService';

// Get value with default fallback
const timeout = configService.get('api.timeoutMs', 5000);
const sources = configService.get('shopping.search.defaultSources', ['ebay', 'amazon']);

// In Agent constructors
constructor(config?: AgentConfig) {
  super({
    rateLimit: configService.get('jobs.agent.rateLimit', 30),
    defaultTimeoutMs: configService.get('jobs.agent.timeoutMs', 60000),
    circuitBreakerThreshold: configService.get('jobs.agent.circuitBreakerThreshold', 3),
    ...config
  });
}
```

### Adding New Config Keys

File: `backend/src/services/core/configService.ts`

```typescript
const DEFAULT_CONFIG = {
  // Add in the appropriate section
  
  // ==========================================================================
  // YOUR AGENT
  // ==========================================================================
  'yourAgent.maxResults': 20,
  'yourAgent.cacheMinutes': 30,
  'yourAgent.ai.maxTokens': 2000,
  'yourAgent.feature.enabled': true,
} as const;
```

### Naming Convention

```
category.subcategory.setting

Examples:
- agent.default.rateLimit
- jobs.agent.timeoutMs
- shopping.ai.maxTokens
- cache.products.ttlSeconds
- feature.israeliShops
```

